+# The Daily Grind
+
+Coffee shop homepage with a passwordless **My Account** area (`/account`) built on passkeys (WebAuthn).
+
+## Running
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm start          # http://localhost:11222
+pnpm test           # end-to-end API tests with a software authenticator
+```
+
+| Env var     | Default                        | Purpose                                                        |
+| ----------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `PORT`      | `11222`                        | HTTP port                                                      |
+| `RP_ID`     | `localhost`                    | WebAuthn relying party ID (your domain, e.g. `dailygrind.com`) |
+| `ORIGIN`    | `http://localhost:$PORT`       | Comma-separated origins the site is served from                |
+| `DATA_FILE` | `data/db.json`                 | Where customers and passkeys are stored                        |
+
+Passkeys only work on `localhost` or over HTTPS, and the page must be opened on one of the `ORIGIN`s
+(e.g. use `http://localhost:11222`, not `http://127.0.0.1:11222`). In production set e.g.
+`RP_ID=dailygrind.com ORIGIN=https://dailygrind.com`. With HTTPS origins, cookies become
+`Secure` / `__Host-` prefixed.
+
+## Passkey features
+
+- **Registration** – name + email, then a discoverable passkey is created (`residentKey: required`). No password.
+- **Sign-in** – usernameless: the "Sign in with a passkey" button, or passkey **autofill** in the email
+  field (conditional mediation). Session IDs are rotated on sign-in.
+- **Saved passkeys** – list (provider name, synced/backed-up badge, created/last used, which one this session
+  used), add more (`excludeCredentials` prevents duplicates per authenticator), rename, remove (the last
+  passkey can't be removed).
+- **Profile** – change name and email; the browser's passkey UI is updated via
+  `PublicKeyCredential.signalCurrentUserDetails`.
+- **Reauthentication** – adding/removing a passkey and changing the email require a passkey check with user
+  verification within the last 5 minutes. The UI prompts with a "Confirm it's you" dialog and then
+  continues the action.
+- **Signal API** – stale passkeys are reported with `signalUnknownCredential` (on failed sign-in) and
+  `signalAllAcceptedCredentials` (after sign-in, page load and removal), so password managers stay in sync.
+
+## Layout
+
+- `server/index.js` – starts the HTTP server
+- `server/app.js` – request handler: static files + `/api/*` (sessions, WebAuthn via `@simplewebauthn/server`)
+- `server/store.js` – JSON-file store; `server/aaguids.js` – passkey provider names
+- `public/` – `index.html`, `account.html`, `css/styles.css`, `js/{nav,account,webauthn}.js`
+
+Sessions are kept in memory, so customers need to sign in again after a server restart.
